invariant: INV-26
file: srv_resume.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: srv_resume.c names a traffic-key entry, so a file outside the four
  INV-26 admits would hand AES a key nobody reviewed for it. srv_ticket.c
  is the server's one admitted file, and inv-26-aes-traffic-keys-only
  fails on any other.

--- old
#include "widemul.h"
--- new
#include "widemul.h"
#define SRV_RESUME_TRAFFIC_KEY(k, key) aes_traffic_key_init((k), (key), 32)
static void srv_resume_traffic_key(aes_traffic_key *k, const uint8_t *key) {
    aes_traffic_key_init(k, key, 32);
}
